{"corrections":["Implement the plan.","we should have distinct only when ctrl+c is used when multiple cursors are availiable; otherwise (e.g. something in clipboard from external place/copied before multicursor) each cursor have identical clipboard","if all are ampty and ctrl+c is used - then all have empty clipboard","also change cursor from bold to thin","FULL VS code like multicursors","Match VS Code spreading","Vertical bar","and once you done - monitor PRs until completion, stop only when ALL of them are merged successfully with dev","fix any issues on the way","also update rpi agents to ALWAYS use recommended options when they have questions about plan/feature implementation/correction","Questions: [\"1. Clipboard rules: does your later “Match VS Code spreading” override the earlier requirement that externally copied text be identical at every cursor? Example: external clipboard is “A\\\\nB” and there are two cursors.\\nSpread matching lines (Recommended): Insert A at the first cursor and B at the second; use copied fragments first when their count matches, otherwise matching lines, otherwise the whole text at each cursor.\\nExternal text stays identical: Insert the whole A\\\\nB at both cursors; distribute only fragments recorded by Ctrl+C with multiple editor cursors.\", \"2. What does “FULL VS code like multicursors” include? The current editor permits one cursor per row and shares a preferred column; the original request describes Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down as anchored selection to the same column on the adjacent logical line.\\nComplete editing semantics (Recommended): Support independent positions and preferred columns, multiple cursors on one row, selection merging, movement, editing and undo/redo; preserve existing creation shortcuts and the explicitly requested vertical-selection behavior.\\nOnly original fixes: Limit changes to the requested vertical selection, clipboard rules and thin carets; retain the current cursor model and creation shortcuts.\\nAlso VS Code creation commands: Include complete editing semantics plus VS Code cursor creation shortcuts and gestures; their exact supported set will need to be specified.\", \"3. How should the visual findings unrelated to multicursors be handled? Several involve pre-existing create-table controls, help wrapping, and inconsistent scene fixtures; they are outside the original feature, but the full visual gate rejected them.\\nFeature-related corrections (Recommended): Correct defects caused by or directly tied to this feature; report unrelated existing findings as deferred blockers and preserve their code.\\nAlso repair scene fixtures: Also correct misleading capture fixtures and focus timing, while deferring unrelated production UI defects.\\nResolve every listed finding: Explicitly authorize narrow repairs to all listed production UI defects and scene fixtures so the full visual gate can pass.\"]\nUser response: Use recommended options","Questions: [\"4. Should fragment metadata be recorded only by multicursor Ctrl+C, or also by the existing `cp` command and Ctrl+X? The partial PR currently treats all three as equivalent.\\nEquivalent copy actions (Recommended): Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments; Ctrl+V, `pst`, and terminal paste use the same spreading rules. Cut deletes selected ranges only.\\nOnly Ctrl+C records fragments: `cp` and Ctrl+X write plain clipboard text and clear fragment metadata; subsequent paste may still spread matching lines under your chosen rule.\", \"5. With one cursor and no selection, should Ctrl+C and `cp` preserve Explorer’s current whole-buffer copy behavior? Your explicit empty-clipboard requirement applies when all selections are empty with multiple cursors.\\nKeep whole-buffer copy (Recommended): One unselected cursor copies the whole SQL buffer; multiple entirely empty selections clear the clipboard.\\nCopy the current line: Use VS Code’s unselected single-cursor line copy, while retaining your explicit empty-clipboard override for multiple cursors.\"]\nUser response: I approve recommended options","Questions: [\"1. Clipboard edge case: with multiple cursors and no selected text, should Ctrl+X clear the clipboard like Ctrl+C/cp, or preserve the existing no-op cut behavior?\\nClear clipboard (Recommended): Treat Ctrl+X as an equivalent copy action: record empty fragments, clear the clipboard, and delete nothing.\\nKeep cut as no-op: Leave clipboard and text unchanged when every selection is empty; record cut fragments only when some text is selected.\", \"2. Existing Shift+Up/Down removes a cursor if its target row is occupied. Once multiple cursors per row are supported, should removal require the same target position, or still affect any cursor on that row?\\nMatch position (Recommended): Add at the projected column; remove an existing cursor only at that position, allowing other cursors on the target row.\\nKeep row toggle: Keep the current row-based creation/removal behavior; independent movement may still bring multiple cursors onto one row.\"]\nUser response: Choose both recommended options under the owner's standing policy: (1) Clear clipboard when every multicursor selection is empty; record empty fragments and delete nothing. (2) Match position for Shift+Up/Down toggling; add at the projected column and remove only the cursor at that exact position, preserving other cursors on the row. Proceed through fresh plan review, correction, independent PR review and checks. This is a routine implementation choice, not a protected-policy approval.","Questions: [\"1. Your earlier answer deferred unrelated UI defects, while the later instruction requires a green full visual gate. May this correction make narrow fixture and UI repairs for the confirmed current blockers: coherent invalid/mutation/results/save scenes and Cancel focus; create-table checkbox/removal legibility and type-menu placement; movement-help wrapping; and find-highlight visibility if still failing after the caret fix?\\nMinimum gate repairs (Recommended): Authorize only these confirmed blockers, preserve the multicursor feature, and require every full scene to pass.\\nFeature and fixtures: Allow multicursor and truthful fixture repairs, but leave unrelated production UI unchanged; publication remains blocked if those scenes fail.\\nFeature only: Retain the earlier deferral boundary; repair multicursors and their visuals, with full-gate publication blocked by unrelated failures.\", \"2. The partial implementation draws │ by replacing the SQL character in its terminal cell, hiding the S in SELECT. For terminal rendering, which compromise is acceptable if a thin vertical bar cannot share the same cell with readable text?\\nPreserve text (Recommended): Use a terminal-supported bar where possible, with a thin underline fallback for occupied cells; keep all SQL legible and expose secondary carets.\\nRequire vertical bars: Require vertical bars for all carets and allow a presentation-only extra cell before the character, with matching mouse, scrolling, ruler, and selection mapping.\\nBar may cover text: Keep the cell-replacing bar; the current legibility rejection would remain unresolved and publication blocked.\", \"3. Which PRs does “ALL of them are merged successfully with dev” cover? The supplied feature evidence identifies PR #9; companion evidence mentions other PRs but does not establish their task membership.\\nTask-related PRs (Recommended): Monitor #9 and every correction or repair PR created for this SQL Explorer task through successful dev merge and required validation.\\nAll currently open PRs: Include every currently open repository PR; the coordinator must record the live inventory and preserve each PR’s separate scope and approval requirements.\\nExplicit PR list: Use a specific set supplied in the free-text answer, plus their task-related correction and repair PRs.\"]\nUser response: also update rpi agents to ALWAYS use recommended options when they have questions about plan/feature implementation/correction","Questions: []\nUser response: also update rpi agents to ALWAYS use recommended options when they have questions about plan/feature implementation/correction","Questions: []\nUser response: also restart agents who are waiting user's approval so that use this new policy","Coordinator-provided fresh diagnostic evidence is now available through source_files. GitHub capture https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/actions/runs/38731476440 succeeded for exact candidate 3e6d6e980ea7f1e1c3a6412cb9c5cc824aa87df5. Its artifact patch matches your current saved checkpoint: SHA256 a3c095c05168e2ed96ae63653c93a579baef3bad0d6a73ecff30df9b1fdd4141.\n\nQuestion: “Can the coordinator expose a fresh database-picker capture with its heading widget rows, compositor rows, exported SVG, and hash-bound final PNG through source_files evidence? The available layer evidence is historical, and its PNG is inaccessible. The reviewed plan requires identifying the first failing layer before changing picker presentation or capture/export.”\n\nCoordinator response:\n\n- Immutable evidence prefix: `operator/pr9-baseline-38731476440/`. All 46 full scene PNGs and geometry JSON files are included.\n- Read `database-picker.json` at that prefix, SHA256 `448bc635e4d189a90747d38a2a4793cd2bba386bb57cbc1e29bfd4410def9a35`. Its `render_diagnostics` contains complete heading widget/compositor rows, parsed exported SVG elements, styles, clips and transforms, plus raw/framed SVG and final PNG hashes.\n- Open `database-picker.png` using the newly available read-only `read_evidence_image` tool with SHA256 `01ad7b5da45db751e023aff86610ca6eaeabf90efe8c8c6a89d661bf5b3644b5`. The tool verifies the immutable manifest and actual PNG bytes. It is active in reviewed worker commit 0d987a81510eb945170e45ead87e6ba8b849ae23, exact-commit CI https://github.com/Karapsin/self_host/actions/runs/38731488179 .\n- Start with `operator/pr9-baseline-38731476440/coordinator-receipt.json`, SHA256 1597127f4647b20364f506fc43e6dad323d45c7051e0c1b029100c39fd6fb9e5. This binds the run, candidate, checkpoint and all artifact hashes.\n\nThe deployed capture workflow uploads parsed SVG diagnostics in JSON; it does not upload separate raw SVG files. Do not claim raw SVG bytes are supplied. Inspect the actual diagnostics and PNG to identify the first failing layer before changing presentation or export. If raw SVG bytes remain essential, identify that remaining coordinator artifact-export gap; these files are generated diagnostics, not replacements for owner images. No owner answer, policy approval or visual-review pass is manufactured by this coordinator response.","Coordinator tooling update: your previous capture response was accepted. Planning then paused before invoking a model because the trusted PR-body renderer exceeded its 55,000-character transport limit; the stored question list is empty. No new owner decision is needed for that size error.\n\nThe reviewed worker fix in self_host commit 2273123fac5bf806446907b1f7c705786991c117 now validates the complete task schema before planning/coding without requiring it to fit a PR body. It preserves every original prompt, plan, question and answer. Publication still preflights the trusted renderer before enrollment, push, PR writes or hold recovery, and retains the exact artifact if the current transport is too small. A larger lossless publication transport remains a coordinator repair; do not truncate history or claim that transport is already implemented.\n\nExact-commit CI passed: https://github.com/Karapsin/self_host/actions/runs/38734363567 . Source review and separate rollout review approved this change. Continue fresh planning and independent review using the actual capture diagnostics already supplied at https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/pull/9#issuecomment-6191690770 . The original SQL Explorer scope and all provenance, visual review and owner-policy gates remain unchanged.\n\nThis is a transparent coordinator status/evidence response to the recorded transport blocker, not an invented owner answer, replacement image, plan approval or protected-policy approval.","Coordinator tooling repair is active. self_host commit 8dcf886114f5ed53144e053e9fcb5921bfb2e74e fixes both native planning gaps: read_evidence_image results now arrive as native inputImage items, and old durable threads with outdated dynamic tool definitions rotate to a fresh read-only thread exposing the current tools. Previous thread questions and plan provenance are archived; your complete authenticated task/question/answer history remains in the new turn prompt. No old requestUserInput RPC answer is replayed.\n\nSource review and separate activation review approved the exact change. Required exact-commit CI and isolated rollout/restart/rollback tests passed: https://github.com/Karapsin/self_host/actions/runs/38736868724 . The worker is active; all 78 saved checkpoints and the existing orchestrator cadence were verified unchanged. Installed-source receipt: operator/worker-native-tools-8dcf886114f5-active.json in assigned immutable evidence.\n\nContinue fresh native planning and inspect the hash-bound PNG from operator/pr9-baseline-38731476440/ using read_evidence_image with the exact hash declared in your immutable manifest. The capture receipt still binds candidate 3e6d6e980ea7f1e1c3a6412cb9c5cc824aa87df5 to the saved checkpoint. Widget/compositor/parsed-SVG diagnostics are available; raw SVG bytes were not supplied. Establish whether the PNG actually shows a production UI or export defect before selecting a correction. Keep the original user scope, full history, original plan and authentic approvals; this is a coordinator tooling response, not a replacement image or approval.\n\nLossless publication transport beyond the current body-size limit remains coordinator-owned and pending; do not truncate task history or ask the owner to manufacture replacement evidence for that tooling limit. SQL Explorer changes still require the existing independent visual review and CI gates.","Coordinator evidence-route answer: the deployed main agent-visual.yml currently copies each scene PNG and geometry JSON into visual-artifact, plus capture.json. It does not copy raw or framed SVG sidecars. Candidate 3e6d6e980ea7f1e1c3a6412cb9c5cc824aa87df5 already computes both SVG strings in agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_capture.py before calling render_diagnostics, but the diagnostics retain parsed elements and hashes only. The requested SVG bytes therefore are genuinely absent from the old artifact; no owner upload or replacement decision is needed.\n\nUse the existing trusted candidate-capture path to obtain that missing evidence. A bounded diagnostic instrumentation step in the assigned candidate harness can retain complete raw and framed SVG content in the already-exported scene geometry JSON, with exact byte hashes and an explicit lossless encoding/chunk description if needed. Retain renderer versions and actual available/selected font diagnostics, or explicitly record unavailable probes. Instrumentation and font probes execute only in the GitHub capture job; private source workers must not execute programs, tests or rendering. Keep output bounded and provide enough metadata for the coordinator to verify hashes and extract complete readable evidence from the GitHub artifact. Do not change framing, rasterization or production UI behavior speculatively.\n\nHave renewed planning and independent plan review cover this diagnostic prerequisite while preserving the complete existing feature checkpoint and original SQL Explorer requirements. Once the source-only coding step has supplied that instrumentation, the normal controller visual phase can publish an isolated temporary candidate and run the existing GitHub workflow to collect the data. This is intermediate diagnosis: do not claim the feature or visual review is complete, drop remaining feature work, bypass a rejecting visual gate, or publish a correction before the required full-scene review. Continue correction from the resulting actual evidence. The original context, questions/answers, original plan approvals, task/patch/candidate binding and all owner-policy gates remain intact.\n\nThis is a transparent coordinator capability and routing response, not a substitute owner answer, fabricated SVG evidence or plan/policy approval.","Exact pre-invocation source is recovered and assigned as immutable evidence. tests/agent_tools/render_diagnostics.py has identical bytes in the retained 20-code, 22-plan and fresh read-only 23-plan-review workspaces: SHA256 a03170ba8c7073d9742d1ba23b30b1dcc24ce67091e8bf91a7ff22189af1ba0a, 23,459 bytes, 536 lines. The 24-code version is 309 lines and differs, confirming the lost suffix. Read operator/pr9-pre24-source/tests/agent_tools/render_diagnostics.py completely, including lines 301-536, before restoring the omitted source and retaining your focused diagnostic additions. This is original checkpoint source, not an owner replacement.\n\nThe original agent_tools/README.md is also assigned at operator/pr9-pre24-source/agent_tools/README.md: SHA256 e5da7d2d6845ec54a700dc3dcfa6c4db3ba4445f9caf36a1e73266474344c0ba, 32,685 bytes, 494 lines. Use it to verify every current change, preserving all original content and intended new diagnostic documentation. The coordinator's byte-bound comparison and provenance are recorded at operator/pr9-pre24-source/receipt.json (SHA256 dee8e0965575263da28456078bacbbd502862c98853beb5ad964ab3ff76110fc). Read paginated evidence to the actual final line; current tools cap a read at 300 lines and 24,000 characters, so a requested larger count is not proof of complete reading. The source tool's incomplete-read overwrite protection is being repaired separately; do not claim that guard is deployed yet.\n\nPreserve the complete current checkpoint and new SVG-evidence helper/tests, original feature scope, all questions/answers and original plan approvals. Restore only accidental omissions; do not reset the whole patch or discard useful new work. Then continue the approved diagnostic prerequisite and the ordinary GitHub candidate-capture/full visual-review path. No source programs, tests or rendering on the Pi. No owner answer or protected policy approval is supplied by this coordinator recovery response.","The requested diagnostic capture is complete. The trusted controller published only temporary candidate 80327049f169cc636a6638b7a17337eecd2c0de4 from the exact preserved checkpoint SHA256 d2ddb31be4c513d4b1b2ea6284760e2d0460c70190445cd5c59a448450ad6d38. GitHub visual run https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/actions/runs/38753763726 succeeded. All 46 PNG and geometry hashes were verified; the recovered diagnostic tests remain present (545 lines, original test methods retained).\n\nRead immutable evidence under operator/pr9-svg-diagnostics-38753763726/. coordinator-receipt.json SHA256 ca5b50bbbad3e895027fa792b14061c4337bccaf1c2afa28e1a4e59be8a0ca21 binds the request, checkpoint, candidate, plan, GitHub workflow and file hashes. database-picker.json SHA256 f2cb49ae6f34c7600d50d73d361652a1ad1368dd45b5c1a4401023353e9bc8d2 contains the original complete export_input_evidence. Its exact decoded UTF-8 SVG strings were losslessly extracted as database-picker-raw-svg.svg SHA256 373825062510e34c8a6b757418db66642c26ff5ec2d483e35c51b71d440819ac and database-picker-framed-svg.svg SHA256 9c6c4cc55177b9fd117c5d412e62c12d43aa595e911e8a92f7f5a1d2a20aa5b5. Read every relevant page using next_start_line/next_start_column until has_more=false; no source content was normalized or replaced.\n\nThe explicit font/renderer subset is database-picker-font-renderer.json SHA256 591867b1a0d27300e830c1ee181746131a084c99060a2376b74688d57f95501f. It records Python 3.11.17, Textual 0.73.0, Rich 15.0.0, resvg-py 0.5.0, requested font families, actual fc-list and fc-match observations. The actual renderer-selected font is explicitly unobservable through this resvg-py API; do not mistake a system font match for proof of renderer selection. This is the actual available diagnostic, not a guessed selection or owner-supplied replacement.\n\nOpen the full PNG using read_evidence_image(path=\"operator/pr9-svg-diagnostics-38753763726/database-picker.png\", sha256=\"01ad7b5da45db751e023aff86610ca6eaeabf90efe8c8c6a89d661bf5b3644b5\"). The heading defect is still visible; this successful diagnostic run is not a final visual approval or claim of repair. Only database-picker includes the new SVG/font instrumentation; all scene PNGs and geometry are retained.\n\nUse this evidence for the existing approved diagnostic prerequisite and continue the original UI correction without weakening feature scope, provenance, tests, or visual gates. Preserve all original questions/answers, plan approval and useful checkpoint edits. Complete-read safeguards and hash-bound edit_file are now active. No programs, tests or rendering on the Pi. No owner decision or protected policy approval is supplied by this coordinator evidence response.","Choose Evidence first (Recommended), following independent plan resolution under the owner's standing policy. Preserve the complete feature checkpoint, task history, multicursor/clipboard/caret requirements and selected narrow UI repairs. Make behavior-preserving Ruff/format corrections and add bounded failing-state diagnostics plus focused task-related regressions. Obtain exact-head GitHub reproduction and coverage JSON before choosing a checkbox production repair; preserve all assertions and coverage/debt baselines. Retain the unresolved picker comparison prerequisite. Private workers execute no tests or rendering. Continue fresh independent plan review, implementation review, full visual review and required CI. This selects the correction sequence only; it supplies no missing evidence or source, visual, protected-policy or merge approval. Record this question and answer together.\n\nQuestion being answered (verbatim):\n1. The current logs prove checkbox text loss but do not identify its first failing layer; they also report coverage totals without exact missing arcs. Which correction sequence should the plan use?\nEvidence first (Recommended): Fix behavior-preserving Ruff/format issues, add bounded failing-state diagnostics and focused task-related regressions, and obtain exact-head GitHub reproduction plus coverage JSON before selecting a checkbox production repair.\nSeparate diagnostic checkpoint: Keep this step diagnostic-only; obtain checkbox state and coverage evidence on GitHub, then independently plan all lint, test and production corrections together.\n\nResolution: approved by independent plan resolver /root/resolve_pr9_ci_sequence, bound to complete request SHA256 24d5c1a15121516c37a9fabf930c9db886e9a3b6a4a226c81ba05d41d6e9a52a. Posted transparently under the owner's explicit authorization to answer agents; no new owner fact is asserted.","Automated coordinator response under the user's standing authorization, independently checked by the plan resolver. These are coordinator evidence gaps; no owner upload or preference is needed.\n\n1. Picker evidence is now available. Read operator/pr9-e324-rendering/index.json using read_evidence_file with evidence_kind=\"companion\" and SHA256 a9676022d40e8f1863f3523abf7056c450d4c93aa3bb21b7c4ec2e01c18aac48. Use the ordinary companion evidence tools, including read_evidence_image; the separate visual channel is not assigned to this planner. Follow every text continuation until complete.\n\nThe index binds capture 38927473247, head e3246e88769588cf10b61b5d8de3de1193c43ba2, task digest 65fce6603a35c48eb87d766035541debf26341487cc16c53fb435762d13142ad and review-execution-bound visual manifest 282b088c706ab7f41ef1868ef0312952909e361008ceafc74c67627e8e9ce9ef. It provides the receipt, capture metadata, complete original geometry in three exact ordered parts, navigable geometry sections, complete raw/framed SVGs and all four comparison PNGs. Each packet file fits the ordinary evidence limit. This preserves observed bytes; it supplies no visual or implementation approval. The source heading finding remains unresolved despite scene passes. Inspect the actual comparisons before selecting the export repair.\n\n2. The original coverage JSON is unavailable. The coordinator verified run 38927048857 has no retained artifacts. Its complete quality log confirms JSON generation and reports 13225/13492 branches, 98.02% against 98.03%, with 267 missing. Missing arcs cannot be reconstructed from totals. Do not invent them or call a future report the original run's report.\n\n3. The requested pre-assert type-menu trace was not retained. Existing failed-job logs do not supply that bounded runtime observation. Do not assume fixture timing or a production positioning cause.\n\nProceed with a concrete evidence-first plan for fresh independent plan review. Its initial coding step may add bounded, non-mutating failure diagnostics capturing focus, type_input, matches, scroll offsets, field/viewport geometry and queued layout state immediately before the existing assertion, plus meaningful focus/viewport regression instrumentation and retention of canonical coverage JSON through the normal GitHub artifact route. Preserve strict assertions and the 98.03% coverage floor. Run diagnostics only through GitHub, binding new evidence to its actual source, candidate, dependencies and run.\n\nUse the supplied picker comparisons immediately; obtain missing menu and coverage observations through that reviewed diagnostic step. Once evidence identifies the failing layer and missing arcs, independently plan the narrow repair and task-related regressions. Preserve the full feature checkpoint, authenticated history and original requirements. Private workers execute no programs, tests or rendering. Retain fresh implementation review, full-scene visual review, required CI and applicable protected approval. This intermediate sequence does not complete the task or authorize merging. Record this full question and response together.","Choose Preserve whitespace (Recommended). Render a thin underline for every in-document whitespace cell, including existing spaces and all expanded-tab cells, for both primary and secondary carets. Reserve vertical bars for end-of-line or empty-line padding; preserve the already-selected occupied-text underline fallback. Keep the underlying SQL, whitespace characters, colors, cell widths, cursor/selection/scroll/ruler mapping and completion behavior unchanged. Add focused primary/secondary space/tab rendering and completion regressions, then obtain fresh independent plan review before coding. Preserve the complete multicursor/selection/clipboard/history feature and authenticated history, GitHub-only validation, all 46 scene geometry/full-PNG verdicts, independent implementation review, exact-head CI and applicable protected approval gates. This selects the routine implementation option under the user's standing authorization; it is not a visual pass, source/plan/policy approval, merge clearance or invented owner fact.\n\nQuestion and options being answered (verbatim):\n1. The rejected PNG and widget/compositor rows show `SELECT c.c│FROM`: rendering replaces the existing separator space with a bar. Should the correction preserve every in-document whitespace cell using the thin underline fallback, reserving vertical bars for end-of-line and empty-line padding?\nPreserve whitespace (Recommended): Keep spaces and expanded tabs intact for primary and secondary carets; retain colors, cell widths and completion behavior, and add focused rendering and completion regressions.\n\nTransparent coordinator response under the owner’s standing authorization to answer aligned recommended implementation choices. A separate independent plan resolver checked the complete retained task (digest 89b22e211df928be606edce5322bfaf17a6c2da89645af7df53dd6f0f3df9919); resolution SHA256 9df1177c9ebbaa5d7e0c0437e91808fb83e4962f4a51cbdd070d7ab52109e532. This is an automated implementation-choice response, not a new personal owner fact or protected/visual approval.","Select Preserve dev safeguards (Recommended). This is an independently checked routine reconciliation with the newly assigned dev base under the owner’s standing implementation/repair instructions. Restore the inherited capture exporter, its regressions and parent-objective record, and agent-visual workflow exactly from the immutable pinned dev; retain all dev capture documentation plus the feature-specific activation section. Preserve the complete SQL Explorer patch and original task/evidence. Then obtain fresh current-base plan assessment, independent complete-feature review, exact-head GitHub fast checks and every required complete visual review. This supplies no new owner fact, policy approval, hold release, CI result or visual pass. Retain all protected/provenance/dependency gates and the all-qualifying-PR successful-dev-merge objective.\n\nCoordinator response under the owner’s standing instruction to answer implementation questions in GitHub. A separate read-only assessment selected the recommended option; this is not a new owner fact or policy approval.\n\nQuestion and all options:\n\n1. Should the plan restore the newly pinned dev’s capture/export safeguards before completing the outstanding independent review? The current diff deletes `.github/agent/capture_artifact.py`, its regression module and a parent-objective record, reverts `agent-visual.yml`, and removes failed-capture documentation.\nPreserve dev safeguards (Recommended): Restore those files and workflow exactly from pinned dev, retain its documentation plus the feature-specific activation section, preserve the complete SQL Explorer patch, then obtain fresh review and GitHub validation.\nReview before reconciliation: Complete read-only assessment of the published predecessor first; keep current-base reconciliation and final candidate validation blocked until separately planned.\n\nAnswer and reasoning:\n\nSelect Preserve dev safeguards (Recommended). This is an independently checked routine reconciliation with the newly assigned dev base under the owner’s standing implementation/repair instructions. Restore the inherited capture exporter, its regressions and parent-objective record, and agent-visual workflow exactly from the immutable pinned dev; retain all dev capture documentation plus the feature-specific activation section. Preserve the complete SQL Explorer patch and original task/evidence. Then obtain fresh current-base plan assessment, independent complete-feature review, exact-head GitHub fast checks and every required complete visual review. This supplies no new owner fact, policy approval, hold release, CI result or visual pass. Retain all protected/provenance/dependency gates and the all-qualifying-PR successful-dev-merge objective.\n\nIndependent assessment SHA256: `1db30728aff48c3cb1cc4221fe0bf65784a434683242eebe3df095c99d831d73`.\n\nThe earlier comment retained the question context but did not match the handler’s command-first syntax. This comment submits the same authorized answer through the actual parser.","Preserve ruler (Recommended).\n\nTransparent coordinator response following independent read-only alignment assessment by /root/resolve_pr29_compact_test_question under the owner's standing authorization. This selects a correction strategy only, not a new user preference or plan/source/visual/protected-policy approval.\n\nThe complete original feature/history supports preserving ruler, cursor, scroll and text mapping. The actual run 39069364836 full PNG shows the upper label at the text/caret column and a separate lower gutter 1. Its geometry separates the one-row ruler at y3 from the editor beginning at y4. Candidate 98508973146e4137a88eaacff9a4cc13f8e84d9c and pinned dev 7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a ruler bytes are identical, SHA256 7e6c19078683d95c583a28ac4cfefc740ce66ee8f762185b4b3a99c9b102883e; both inherited tests explicitly expect ruler 1 for an empty document. These are grounds for focused regression/evidence and independent reassessment, not a finding-clearance or visual-pass claim.\n\nPreserve production presentation. Independently review the renewed complete plan, then add a real mounted tab/database-switch ruler/gutter regression and explicit scene metadata showing the active column, separate ruler/editor regions and rendered first gutter/text row. Retain every existing assertion and negative control. Give the exact full PNG/geometry/source evidence to the independent reviewer and keep the current rejection/gate in force until fresh independent review resolves it. If new evidence demonstrates a real defect, independently plan that narrow repair rather than forcing this explanation to pass.\n\nRetain the entire original selection/multicursor/clipboard/caret/history feature, all selected UI/fixture and capture repairs, current-dev safeguards, complete context and evidence, all 46 required geometry/full-PNG reviews, exact-head CI, independent full-feature review, genuine private/protected holds and all qualifying PR successful-dev-merge obligations. This answer releases no dependency or approval gate. Do not alter the frozen rollout sources, rerun completed deployments or execute candidate code/tests/scenes on Pi.\n\nExact question and all offered options:\n1. Should the renewed plan preserve the inherited column ruler and route the reported stray “1” for independent reassessment, using the inspected PNG, separate ruler/editor geometry, identical pinned-dev ruler source, and existing empty-document assertion? This resolves the correction approach only; the rejecting visual gate remains in force until independently reviewed.\nPreserve ruler (Recommended): Preserve production presentation; add a focused tab-switch ruler/gutter regression and explicit scene evidence, then repeat independent full-feature and visual review.\nChange ruler presentation: Authorize a narrow presentation change to distinguish column labels from gutter numbers; its exact appearance needs a further decision before implementation.","Diagnose first (Recommended).\n\nTransparent coordinator response after independent read-only alignment assessment by /root/resolve_pr29_compact_test_question under the owner's standing authorization. This selects the diagnostic sequence only; it is not a new owner fact or plan/source/visual/protected-policy/deployment approval.\n\nThe complete original feature requires visible primary and secondary carets while preserving SQL, whitespace, colors, widths and mapping. The fresh keyboard-multicursor feedback establishes a visibility concern but does not identify the first failing layer. Preserve the complete feature and selected ruler work. After independent review of the complete diagnostic plan, collect bounded, non-mutating GitHub-only cursor/selection/focus/scroll/keyboard state, exact caret-cell widget and compositor text/styles, and lossless SVG evidence with source/task/checkpoint/base/dependency/run/hash bindings and focused regressions. State unavailable or incomplete observations honestly; do not change focus, timing, assertions, production presentation or export behavior to make the diagnostic pass.\n\nUse the actual new evidence to independently plan the narrow demonstrated production or export repair. Inconclusive diagnostics remain unresolved. Retain every existing assertion/negative control, all original editing/clipboard/history and current-dev safeguards, complete questions/options/answers/evidence, the selected ruler regression/reassessment, every genuine protected/private/dependency gate and all qualifying PR successful-dev-merge obligations. Require fresh exact-head CI, complete independent feature review and all 46 candidate-bound geometry/full-PNG verdicts before correction publication. Historical captures cannot certify new edits. No code/tests/scenes run on Pi and no completed deployment is rerun.\n\nExact question and all offered options:\n1. Should the renewed plan first collect bounded, GitHub-only evidence for the indistinct secondary carets before choosing a production or export repair? The inspected PNG confirms the visibility finding, but its geometry does not identify the failing layer.\nDiagnose first (Recommended): Preserve the complete feature and selected ruler work; add exact cursor/focus/scroll state, caret-cell widget/compositor styles and lossless SVG evidence with focused regressions, then independently plan the demonstrated repair after GitHub capture.\nChange caret presentation: Plan a production presentation change now; its precise appearance requires another choice and must preserve SQL, whitespace, colors, widths and mapping.\n\nIndependent assessment SHA256: b5b5e378878572299d4533b21d8a1e6d8dd1358f873051a6d62b7c61ce7ba279.","new_visual_blockers: Narrow gate repairs (Recommended)\nReason: The standing instruction to fix issues along the way and the later independent recommendation policy support narrow repairs of demonstrated blockers needed for the complete visual gate. The retained history already settled Minimum gate repairs and separately extended that enumerated boundary through an evidence-led picker-heading repair. The present choice similarly names only journal failure reporting and restoring existing intended new-file alignment after identifying the failing layers. It preserves the complete feature, adds focused regressions and retains all review gates. It is consistent with reliable completion rather than a new product or presentation redesign. An evidence-led plan must establish the actual layer and intended placement before coding; this assessment does not independently certify the supplied newly verified findings. Do not broaden this into unrelated UI work or infer source/visual acceptance.\n\ndiagnostic_ci_correction: Faithful diagnostics (Recommended)\nReason: Preserving complete multicursor/caret behavior requires diagnostic bytes and styles to reflect the actual state, including combining marks, cell styles, crop mapping and command/ruler lifecycle. Bounded variable-shadowing/lint corrections and faithful cropping address the reported diagnostic/test failures while retaining every strict assertion and negative control. Collecting missing command-caret and ruler focus/width evidence on GitHub before choosing further presentation or focus changes follows the retained Diagnose first and Preserve ruler decisions. Do not force focus, timing, width, caret state or scene state to pass. Unknown observations remain unknown; any demonstrated repair requires fresh full-scope independent planning and normal validation.\n\nTransparent automated coordinator response after separate independent full-task assessment under the owner's standing authorization. Both choices settle only the renewed-plan strategy and narrow scope. Retain original anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection, complete independent/same-row multicursors, exact-position toggles, clipboard fragment/line/whole-text precedence and empty-selection rules, atomic history/pruning/reset, thin primary/secondary underline carets in all occupied/space/tab cells with bars only in padding, and unchanged SQL/text/colors/widths/mapping/completion. Preserve selected ruler presentation/reassessment, current-dev capture/provenance safeguards, recovered source/docs, the complete useful checkpoint, all existing UI/fixture/export/supersampling repairs and their evidence. Preserve coverage/debt floors, every strict assertion and negative control. Obtain fresh independent whole-plan review before coding, GitHub-only focused and final-head CI, independent complete-feature/source review and all46 candidate-bound geometry and individual full1280x800 PNG verdicts; historical captures cannot validate new edits. Preserve companion recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, exporter/producer-consumer/activation and merge/dependency obligations, including PR10 actual PR9 ancestry. Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs through successful dev merge and required validation for every qualifying PR and resulting repair; no leaf fix completes the full objective. Retain notification limits, concurrency10, truthful lifecycle labels including agent:writing, complete question/options/answer records, authenticated GitHub/Telegram responses, single30-minute/open-PR orchestrator and idle exit, and GitHub-agent-only self_host relevance. Retain all credentials/authentication/provenance/security limits, genuine owner input, veto/cancel and protected exact-head holds. This grants no new owner fact, plan/source/visual/protected/deployment approval or merge clearance. Execute no candidate programs/tests/scenes on Pi, do not modify frozen rollout sources or rerun completed deployments, and preserve the coordinator-owned drain pause. Coordinator evidence acquisition and future work must use normal reviewed isolated GitHub mechanisms.\n\nExact questions and offered options:\n\n1. May the renewed plan include narrow repairs for the newly verified journal-error status and new-file dialog alignment, after identifying their failing layers? These extend the earlier enumerated UI repair scope.\nNarrow gate repairs (Recommended): Show read failures without claiming empty results, restore intended dialog centering, add focused regressions, and retain the complete feature and all review gates.\n\n2. Should the correction fix the confirmed diagnostic/test defects and collect missing command-caret and ruler lifecycle evidence before selecting further presentation or focus changes?\nFaithful diagnostics (Recommended): Fix variable shadowing and lint, preserve combining marks and cell styles during cropping, retain strict assertions, and diagnose ruler focus/width and command-caret layers on GitHub without forcing scene state.","ruler_correction_sequence: Trace lifecycle (Recommended)\nReason: The complete task and retained Preserve ruler/Faithful diagnostics decisions require preserving the inherited production ruler, actual observed focus/state, exact widget/compositor equality, all assertions and negative controls. The available log records editor focus where command focus was expected, and a Python3.14/Textual0.89.1 ruler observation with205widget cells versus206compositor cells; those snapshots establish the failures, not callback order or the first strip-padding divergence. Bounded GitHub-only lifecycle and padding observations before selecting a behavioral correction therefore align with the existing evidence-led sequence and avoid forcing focus, widths or scene state just to make tests pass. Behavior-preserving fixes for the reported PLR0911 and formatting findings are in scope while retaining diagnostic output, meaningful regressions and quality/coverage baselines. Preserve the newly pinned current-dev safeguards at f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01; older7142 plans and captures cannot validate this base or current unpublished edits. The alternative command-focus-after-tab/full-width collection approach can be independently planned only if fresh evidence demonstrates that correction, rather than being selected from snapshot symptoms alone. No new owner fact, preference, upload or authority is required for this diagnostic strategy.\n\nTransparent automated coordinator response after separate independent full-task assessment under the owner's standing recommended-options policy. This selects the correction sequence only. Obtain fresh independent review of the complete current-base plan before coding; collect bounded non-mutating GitHub-only observations of callback scheduling/execution, tab restoration/focus transitions, original/rendered strip lengths/padding and relevant versions, with actual source/checkpoint/candidate/base/task/plan/dependency/run/hash bindings. Keep first failing-state evidence, unavailable or incomplete observations and strict equality/negative controls intact; do not recollect until assertions pass, strip expected spaces, force focus/width, add event-draining/timing retries, change ruler presentation or weaken any gate. Use demonstrated evidence to independently plan the narrow correction, and retain unresolved findings if diagnosis is inconclusive.\n\nPreserve the entire original anchored selection/multicursor/clipboard/caret/history/reset feature: Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selection without new cursors; independent and same-row cursors, preferred columns and exact-position toggles; fragment/matching-line/whole-text paste rules and empty-selection overrides; atomic undo/redo and bounded metadata/reset cleanup; thin primary/secondary underlines in existing text/spaces/expanded tabs and bars only in padding, preserving SQL, colors, widths and all selection/scroll/ruler/completion mapping. Retain selected narrow UI/fixture/journal/new-file repairs, faithful combining-mark/style cropping, current-dev safeguards, supersampling/capture evidence, recovered source/docs and complete useful checkpoint. Retain coverage/debt floors, every meaningful assertion/negative control, GitHub focused/final-head quality/type/artifact/compatibility/fast checks, independent complete-feature/source review and all46 candidate-bound geometry and individual full1280x800 PNG verdicts at208x47. Historical evidence cannot certify new content.\n\nKeep companion recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, exporter/producer-consumer/activation/rollback and dependency requirements, including PR10 actualPR9 merge ancestry, and monitor every qualifying PR/resulting repair through successfuldevmerge and required postmergevalidation. Preserve notification limits, concurrency10, truthful lifecycle labels including agent:writing, completeQ/options/A, authenticated GitHub/Telegram responses, independent full-taskresolver, single30minute/open-PR orchestrator/idleexit and GitHub-agent-onlyself_host relevance. Honor actual current credential/authentication/provenance/security/owner-veto/cancel/protected holds and coordinator-owned runtime/drain state; historical pause statements do not establish a current pause or authorize clearing/recreating one. Do not alter frozen rollout bytes or rerun completed deployments. No candidate programs/tests/scenes run onPi. This is not a new owner preference, plan/source/visual/protected/deployment approval, merge clearance or broader completion claim.\n\nExact question and all options:\n1. Which correction sequence should the renewed plan specify for the observed ruler focus and row-width failures? Existing assertions and production ruler presentation must remain intact.\nTrace lifecycle (Recommended): Fix the confirmed lint/format findings, preserve current-dev safeguards, and add bounded GitHub-only callback-order and strip-padding observations before selecting the focus or width correction.\nCorrect scene lifecycle: Plan command focus after tab restoration and full-width widget-row collection now; retain strict equality and negative controls, then require GitHub reproduction and independent review.\n\nIndependent resolution SHA256 15319f47a5b173c9a4958e6c711524656f7d8077558f3a0f8a80b376d8b00c86.","ruler_harness_correction: Correct harness layers (Recommended)\nReason: The complete task and selected Trace lifecycle sequence required actual evidence before choosing a correction, preserved production tab/ruler behavior and retained strict diagnostics/assertions. The new exact-head assigned GitHub evidence now goes beyond the earlier snapshots: both Python3.11/Textual0.73.0 andPython3.13/Textual0.89.1 contain complete17-event/no-omission traces showing deferred tab-focus restoration still pending after scene database switching and command-focus initialization, followed by final editor focus. Exact published-head source calls tab activation then immediate command focus; tab activation defers restore_active_focus and workspace restoration focuses the remembered editor. Both matched upstream framework versions apply Widget.focus through call_later, explaining why the callback can return before its focus request takes effect. Separately, the0.89.1 observation preserves a205-cell raw ruler strip and206-cell compositor strip with one additional styled padding cell. Exact source currently calls raw render_line for the widget, while Textual's compositor uses render_lines, whose native styles cache adjusts content width and adds styling/padding. These source-and-trace facts support ordered scene initialization and matching native styled-row/compositor comparison as narrow harness-layer corrections. Preserve unpadded raw observations separately; do not fabricate padding or weaken comparisons. The strategy follows the earlier evidence-first condition; it does not authorize production focus/presentation changes or claim the proposed implementation has passed GitHub validation.\n\nTransparent automated coordinator response after separate independent full-task and evidence assessment under the owner's standing recommended-options policy. This selects the narrow correction strategy only; obtain a fresh separate review of the complete renewed plan before coding. Apply the scene's already intended command focus only as ordered initialization after deferred tab restoration and queued focus application, before readiness/capture. Keep production tab restoration and ruler code/presentation unchanged and retain independent production behavior coverage. Do not repeatedly refocus after evidence collection, retry until assertions pass, sleep/drain arbitrary queues, bypass readiness or silently alter scenario meaning. Prove scene initialization ordering and subsequent observation non-mutation with focused GitHub regressions.\n\nCollect actual native styled widget rows through the framework rendering path and compare them strictly to compositor rows in the same coordinates and complete cell width. Account for widget/content origin, gutter, border, padding and clipping exactly once; require unchanged text, cell lengths and relevant styles. Retain original render_line strips, exact trailing spaces/styles/lengths and first-failure trace as separately identified raw evidence, preserving schema meaning or explicitly documenting compatible additive fields. Keep raw-versus-original-source fidelity assertions as well as strict styled-versus-compositor equality; no strip/rstrip/ljust/manual padding or changed expected number to manufacture equality. Retain all existing overlap, shifted mapping, missing label/gutter and other negative controls; extend them meaningfully to the compared styled layer rather than dropping coverage. Correct confirmed lint/format findings without output changes, suppressions, relaxed debt/coverage floors or lost assertions. Validate the corrected harness onGitHub across bothTextual lines and supported matrix; preserve complete failures/logs and candidate/base/task/plan/dependency/run/hash bindings. Inconclusive or contradictory evidence remains unresolved and requires further independent planning.\n\nPreserve the entire original selection/multicursor/clipboard/caret/history/reset feature, independent preferred columns/same-row cursors/exact-position toggles, fragment/matching-line/whole-text paste and empty-selection semantics, atomic undo/redo and bounded metadata, thin primary/secondary underlines over text/spaces/expandedtabs with bars only inpadding, and unchangedSQL/colors/widths/selection-scroll-ruler-completion mapping. Retain selected narrowUI/fixture/journal/newfile/export/supersampling repairs, faithful diagnostic combining-mark/style cropping, current-dev safeguards atf66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01, recovered source/docs, full useful checkpoint and historical evidence. Keep every quality/coverage/debt floor and meaningful assertion, independent complete-plan/feature/source review, focused/finalheadGitHubCI and all46geometry/individual full1280x800PNG verdicts at208x47 before correction publication. No old capture certifies new edits.\n\nKeep recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, exporter/producer-consumer/activation/rollback and actualmerge/ancestry dependencies, includingPR10/PR9. Continue monitoring and aligned repairs until everyqualifyingPR/resultingrepair merges successfully intodev with requiredvalidation. Retain notificationlimits, concurrency10, truthful lifecyclelabels includingagent:writing, completeQ/options/A, authenticatedGitHub/Telegram responses, full-task independentresolver, single30minute/open-PRorchestrator/idleexit andGitHub-agent-onlyself_hostrelevance. Genuine credentials/authentication/provenance/security, owner-veto/cancel/protected exacthead and actualcurrentoperational holds remain binding. No ownerfact/preference, plan/source/visual/CI/protected/deployment approval, mergeclearance or broadercompletion is supplied. Do not alter frozenrolloutbytes, override quiescence/drain or rerun completeddeployments; no candidate programs/tests/scenes/installs run locally or onPi.\n\nExact question and all options:\n1. Should the renewed plan correct the demonstrated harness-layer mismatch: apply the scene’s intended command focus after deferred tab restoration, and compare Textual’s styled widget rows with compositor rows while retaining the original unpadded strips as separate evidence? Production tab behavior and ruler presentation would stay unchanged; strict equality, negative controls, and all feature/review gates remain required.\nCorrect harness layers (Recommended): Use ordered scene initialization and native styled-row collection, preserve raw observations, fix confirmed lint/format findings, and validate on GitHub.\nExtend diagnostics first: Preserve the failing harness and collect native styled-row and focus-application traces on GitHub before separately planning its correction.\n\nIndependent resolution SHA256 359cd9e3880f4866ded2ac63a3306c838b2a4c02fa6331500cd14562907614d6."],"decisions":[{"choice":"ui_repair_scope: Minimum gate repairs (Recommended)\nReason: The later authenticated standing instruction to always use recommended implementation/correction options supports the previously presented minimum gate repairs, superseding the earlier deferral for these listed blockers. Preserve the multicursor requirements and require every full visual scene to pass through GitHub validation.\ncaret_fallback: Preserve text (Recommended)\nReason: The later standing recommendation policy supports this explicitly presented rendering compromise: vertical bars where supported, thin underlines in occupied cells, and readable SQL with visible primary and secondary carets. It supersedes the earlier unconditional vertical-bar preference for this limitation.\nmonitored_pr_scope: Task-related PRs (Recommended)\nReason: The standing recommendation policy supports the task-related interpretation of ALL PRs. This choice retains the root monitoring objective across SQL Explorer #9, the requested RPi policy/restart companion work, and all related correction or repair PRs until successful dev merge and validation; a leaf repair cannot replace that objective. Protected exact-head approvals remain with the real owner.","questions":["1. Which UI repair scope should the plan retain? Your earlier answer deferred unrelated UI defects; the later questions about broader visual-gate repairs received no direct answer, and partial code cannot establish scope.\nMinimum gate repairs (Recommended): Include only the listed scene consistency/Cancel focus, create-table legibility/type-menu placement, help wrapping, and remaining find-highlight blockers; require the full visual gate.\nFeature and fixtures: Allow multicursor corrections and truthful scene fixtures; defer unrelated production UI repairs even if they block the full visual gate.\nFeature only: Limit corrections to multicursor behavior and visuals; leave unrelated fixtures and UI defects deferred.","2. When a thin vertical caret cannot share a terminal cell with readable SQL, which rendering compromise should the plan use? The earlier “Vertical bar” answer did not resolve this later limitation.\nPreserve text (Recommended): Use a supported vertical bar where possible and a thin underline in occupied cells; show primary and secondary carets without hiding SQL.\nAlways vertical bars: Add presentation-only cells for vertical bars and adjust mouse, scrolling, ruler, selection, and completion mapping consistently.\nBar may cover text: Allow a cell-replacing vertical bar to hide the character beneath it; the legibility gate may remain blocked.","3. Which PRs must reach successful dev merge before the coordinator stops? Supplied evidence identifies SQL Explorer PR #9 and companion work, but does not establish that every open PR belongs to this task.\nTask-related PRs (Recommended): Track #9, the RPi recommendation-policy/restart companion work, and their task-related correction or repair PRs through review, validation, and successful dev merge.\nAll currently open PRs: Record a fresh repository inventory and monitor every currently open PR, preserving each PR’s separate scope and approval requirements.\nExplicit PR list: Use the repository/PR list you supply in the free-text answer, plus their task-related correction and repair PRs."]},{"choice":"database_heading_scope: Repair heading (Recommended)\nReason: The owner's later standing instruction to use recommended implementation/correction options, together with 'fix any issues on the way,' supports this narrow heading repair beyond the earlier enumerated boundary. Diagnose the reported obstruction before treating its cause as confirmed; retain the focused regression and complete GitHub visual gate. This leaf repair preserves all multicursor requirements and the root objective to monitor task-related PRs through successful dev merge and validation. It grants no protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. Should the plan include a narrow correction for the newly reported database-picker heading, where the initial “c” in “.connections” is obscured, beyond the previously enumerated minimum UI repairs?\nRepair heading (Recommended): Diagnose the widget, compositor and capture evidence; fix only the confirmed text-obscuring cause, add a focused regression, and require the full visual gate.\nKeep prior repair boundary: Preserve the earlier enumerated scope and report the heading as an unresolved visual blocker; publication remains blocked while the scene fails."]},{"choice":"picker_export_repair_strategy: Isolate export defect (Recommended)\nReason: The owner's standing recommendation policy and instruction to fix issues support this evidence-first correction. The hash-verified PNG obscures the c, while widget/compositor rows and parsed SVG retain the complete heading. Obtaining raw/framed SVG bytes and renderer/font diagnostics addresses the remaining coordinator artifact gap without inventing a production picker defect or claiming those bytes already exist. Correct only the demonstrated cause, retain fast regression coverage and full independent visual review on GitHub, and preserve all multicursor, RPi policy/restart, provenance and task-related PR monitoring requirements through successful dev merges and validation. Lossless publication transport remains coordinator-owned; history must remain complete. Protected exact-head approval remains exclusively with the real owner.","questions":["1. The verified PNG obscures the `c`, but widget rows, compositor rows and the parsed SVG preserve the complete heading with visible styling and a containing clip. Which correction strategy should the revised plan specify?\nIsolate export defect (Recommended): Keep picker presentation intact. Have the coordinator obtain raw/framed SVG bytes and renderer/font diagnostics from a GitHub reproduction, then correct the demonstrated export/rasterization cause and add a fast regression before full visual review.\nPresentation workaround: Investigate a narrow picker text-rendering workaround, requiring evidence that it preserves the complete heading and terminal layout; this may change production presentation despite intact widget/compositor output."]},{"choice":"picker_rasterization_diagnosis: Controlled captures (Recommended)\nReason: The standing recommendation policy and authenticated coordinator instructions support bounded GitHub-only diagnostic comparisons before selecting a repair. Comparing unchanged and framed SVG inputs and an explicitly available monospace font can investigate the unresolved rendering cause without assuming the actual renderer-selected font. Preserve exact inputs, settings, hashes, PNGs, checkpoint and production UI; retain independent review, full-scene validation, complete feature requirements, RPi policy/restart work and monitoring of all task-related PRs through successful dev merges and validation. This diagnostic choice grants no plan, code, visual or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. The complete raw and framed SVGs retain the heading, but the PNG remains rejected and the actual renderer font is unknown. Should the next independently reviewed step add bounded GitHub-only comparison captures to distinguish framing/scaling from font shaping before selecting a repair?\nControlled captures (Recommended): Preserve the checkpoint and production UI; compare the same SVG before/after framing and with an explicitly available monospace font, retaining exact inputs, settings, hashes and PNGs for review."]},{"choice":"comparison_artifact_transport: Geometry JSON (Recommended)\nReason: The authenticated coordinator explicitly supports bounded, lossless diagnostic content in the already-exported geometry JSON through the existing GitHub candidate-capture route. Extending that route to the selected controlled comparisons preserves exact SVG/PNG inputs, settings and hashes for independent review without changing the protected workflow. Size limits must mark omitted or incomplete evidence explicitly; incomplete comparisons cannot establish a cause or satisfy review. This choice preserves production behavior, the complete checkpoint and history, all multicursor requirements, RPi policy/restart work, full-scene visual and CI gates, and monitoring of all task-related PRs through successful dev merges and validation. It supplies no missing factual evidence and grants no plan, code, visual or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. The trusted workflow uploads scene PNGs and geometry JSON, but no extra comparison files. How should the already-selected controlled picker comparisons reach independent review?\nGeometry JSON (Recommended): Retain bounded, lossless comparison SVGs and base64 PNGs with settings and hashes in database-picker.json; the coordinator extracts hash-bound images using the existing artifact route.\nSeparate artifact files: Extend the protected capture workflow to upload comparison SVG/PNG sidecars, requiring fresh independent review and real owner approval for that exact protected head."]},{"choice":"picker_comparison_recipe: Four-way comparison (Recommended)\nReason: The authenticated standing recommendation policy and previously selected controlled comparisons support this bounded diagnostic recipe. Supplied font evidence lists DejaVu Sans Mono as available; it does not establish the original renderer-selected font. Run comparisons only in GitHub, changing only the terminal font declaration in diagnostic variants while preserving production rendering and the checkpoint. Retain exact inputs, settings, hashes and lossless PNGs through bounded geometry JSON; failures or omissions remain incomplete evidence. This intermediate diagnosis preserves all multicursor requirements, RPi policy/restart work, full independent visual and CI gates, complete provenance, and monitoring of every task-related PR through successful dev merge and validation. It supplies no repair verdict or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. For the already-selected controlled picker captures and geometry-JSON transport, which concrete comparison recipe should the next plan specify?\nFour-way comparison (Recommended): Render raw and framed SVG with original font declarations, then both with only the terminal font declaration changed to verified-available DejaVu Sans Mono. Preserve text, positions, clips and production rendering; retain exact inputs, settings, hashes and lossless PNGs in bounded geometry JSON, marking failures or omissions incomplete.\nStage comparisons: First capture raw versus framed SVG with original fonts; independently review those results before planning a second capture with an explicitly available monospace font. This needs another diagnostic cycle if framing alone does not explain the defect."]},{"choice":"ci_correction_strategy: CSS reference (Recommended)\nReason: The owner's standing recommendation policy and instruction to fix issues support this bounded CI correction. The existing reference already declares color: $text-disabled in CSS; its plain Color.parse override bypasses Textual's CSS resolution. Removing that override while preserving strict resolved/rendered-color comparisons and negative controls aligns with the requirement not to weaken assertions. Behavior-preserving Ruff fixes also align, provided diagnostic output, production UI, the complete feature checkpoint, provenance and validation gates remain intact. Validation must run on GitHub. Preserve the RPi policy/restart work and root monitoring objective through successful dev merges and required validation for every task-related PR. This assessment grants no plan, code, visual or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. Should this correction use Textual’s existing CSS reference to resolve disabled colors and make behavior-preserving Ruff fixes, while retaining the complete feature checkpoint and all review gates?\nCSS reference (Recommended): Remove the invalid plain-color override; retain strict resolved/rendered-color and negative-control assertions; fix helper/test lint without changing diagnostic output or production UI.\nExplicit CSS parsing: Implement test-side parsing of Textual auto/percentage color values and verify it across supported versions; retain the same strict assertions and behavior-preserving lint fixes."]},{"choice":"ci_fixture_strategy: Complete fixture (Recommended)\nReason: The selector fixture mounts only Select, while create-table diagnostics require #create-table-advanced.collapsed. Mounting a real Collapsible corrects missing fixture context while preserving completeness assertions and the missing-context negative control. Behavior-preserving per-region extraction and formatting align with the authenticated evidence-first correction and standing recommendation policy. Preserve diagnostic contents, assertions, coverage/debt baselines, the complete feature checkpoint, unresolved picker prerequisite, GitHub validation and independent review gates, and monitoring of every task-related PR through successful dev merge and required validation. This choice supplies no plan, code, visual, merge or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. Exact-head CI identifies an incomplete selector fixture, a PLR0912 branch-count finding in terminal_diagnostics, and formatting findings in two diagnostic test modules. Which bounded correction should the plan specify?\nComplete fixture (Recommended): Mount a real advanced-panel Collapsible in the selector fixture; preserve every completeness assertion and missing-context negative control; extract per-region collection into a behavior-preserving helper and format the two reported test modules.\nIsolate selector fixture: Stub only checkbox-context collection in the selector-only test, retain real-scene and missing-context coverage elsewhere, and make the same behavior-preserving branch-count and formatting corrections."]},{"choice":"picker_export_correction: Supersampled export (Recommended)\nReason: The standing recommendation policy and evidence-led heading correction support this bounded export strategy. Hash-bound comparisons show intact native-size headings and degradation at target size with either font; preserving SVG interior bytes does not remove the defect. Pillow is already an agent dependency. Supersampling remains a proposed remedy, requiring exact-candidate GitHub reproduction, focused regression, independent implementation review and all 46 full-scene geometry/PNG verdicts before acceptance. Preserve production UI, feature requirements, history, coverage baselines and protected approval gates.\ntype_menu_fixture_correction: Establish viewport (Recommended)\nReason: Exact-head Python 3.13/3.14 snapshots show the focused field at y=-8 above the viewport starting at y=4, with matching type input and populated matches; production positioning explicitly hides such menus. Establishing a settled visible starting viewport corrects this regression's precondition while retaining menu-visible, placement, scroll-out, focus, unchanged-value and no-query assertions. Preserve production positioning and require GitHub validation across supported environments. Both choices retain the complete multicursor/clipboard/caret scope, RPi policy/restart work and root monitoring objective until every task-related PR merges successfully into dev with required validation.","questions":["1. Which correction should the plan specify for the demonstrated target-size picker rendering defect?\nSupersampled export (Recommended): Render the unchanged framed SVG at 2560×1600, then reduce once to 1280×800 with existing Pillow/Lanczos; require GitHub reproduction and full visual review before accepting the repair.\nFurther diagnostic comparison: Keep ordinary capture unchanged and first collect a GitHub comparison of supersampled reduction against current target-size rendering, then independently plan the demonstrated repair.","2. The failing snapshot shows correct menu hiding for an already offscreen field. Should the regression explicitly establish a settled, visible starting viewport before testing scroll-out behavior?\nEstablish viewport (Recommended): Settle expanded layout, focus the field, scroll it into view without animation, and assert its starting geometry before retaining all menu-visible and scroll-out assertions; preserve production positioning.\nTrace scroll origin first: Add bounded GitHub observations around expansion and focus to identify who scrolls the field offscreen before choosing a fixture or production change."]},{"choice":"pillow_test_dependency: Test dependencies (Recommended)\nReason: The supersampling regression imports PIL directly, while both GitHub matrix install commands and tox latest/min and coverage dependencies omit Pillow. Adding the existing agent-tool range Pillow>=10,<13 to those test environments and applying assertion-preserving formatting is a bounded correction supported by the owner's recommendation policy and instruction to fix issues. Preserve public dependencies, Python 3.8–3.14 compatibility, the complete multicursor/clipboard/caret checkpoint, coverage/debt baselines, authenticated history, independent reviews, full-scene visual review and required exact-head GitHub checks. Retain RPi policy/restart work and monitoring of every task-related PR through successful dev merge and required validation. This selection supplies no plan, code, visual, merge or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. Which bounded correction should the plan specify for the current-head Pillow collection failure and Ruff formatting finding?\nTest dependencies (Recommended): Add Pillow>=10,<13 to both GitHub matrix install commands, tox latest/min test dependencies and tox coverage dependencies; format supersampled_capture.py while preserving all assertions, public dependencies, feature changes and review gates.\nShared test requirements: Introduce a shared test-only Pillow requirements file consumed by those GitHub and tox environments, with the same compatibility range, formatting correction and preserved assertions; this adds a new dependency-management file."]},{"choice":"history_retention_strategy: Shared lifecycle (Recommended)\nReason: The request requires complete multicursor editing and undo/redo semantics and fixing issues encountered. Source confirms cursor edits prune metadata against live undo/redo edits, while indentation appends records without that pruning. Shared recording/pruning, reset cleanup, and regressions for repeated indentation/undo, discarded redo branches, eviction and reset address this defect without reducing feature scope. Preserve cursor selections and preferred columns for live history, the complete checkpoint and authenticated history, GitHub-only validation, independent implementation review, full-scene visual review, coverage/debt baselines and applicable real-owner protected approvals. Retain the RPi recommendation-policy/restart work and root monitoring objective until every task-related PR merges successfully into dev with required validation. This selects an implementation approach only; it grants no plan, code, visual, protected-policy or merge approval.","questions":["1. Which correction should the renewed plan specify for the verified cursor-history retention defect, while preserving the complete feature checkpoint and all review gates?\nShared lifecycle (Recommended): Share recording/pruning across cursor edits and indentation, retain metadata only for live undo/redo edits, clear obsolete records on document resets, and add fast regressions for repeated indent/undo, discarded redo branches, history eviction and reset."]},{"choice":"reset_and_fixture_correction: Reset state (Recommended)\nReason: The request requires complete multicursor editing semantics and fixing encountered issues; the standing policy supports this routine recommended correction. Current load_text clears history snapshots but retains secondary selections and preferred columns. Clearing obsolete cursor state before replacement while preserving Textual’s primary reset behavior addresses that defect. Mounted reset/render/type regressions and complete idle/EditHistory fixtures support validation without weakening assertions. Preserve the complete feature checkpoint, clipboard/caret requirements, history lifecycle, compatibility and coverage baselines. Require GitHub-only validation, fresh independent plan and implementation review, and full-scene visual review bound to the corrected candidate; published-head evidence cannot validate unpublished edits. Retain RPi policy/restart work and monitoring of every task-related PR through successful dev merge and required validation. This resolves the choice only and grants no plan, source, visual, merge or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. Which bounded correction should the renewed plan specify for the verified stale-cursor reset defect and the two CI fixture failures?\nReset state (Recommended): Clear secondary selections and old preferred columns before document replacement, preserve Textual’s primary reset behavior, add mounted reset/render/type regressions, complete the idle test double, and supply all required EditHistory constructor arguments.\nReconcile cursors: Clamp and merge existing cursors into the replacement document instead of clearing them, with explicit retained-cursor tests and the same two CI fixture corrections."]},{"choice":"unmounted_reset_context: Active app context (Recommended)\nReason: The standing recommendation policy and instruction to fix encountered issues support this bounded test-context correction. The existing unmounted reset test constructs two detached editors outside an app context, while neighboring history regressions use asyncio.run and SqlExplorerApp(FakeSession()).run_test(). Providing that context while explicitly preserving both editors' unmounted state and every construction/reset/history assertion retains the required regression coverage without changing production behavior. Preserve the complete feature checkpoint, multicursor/clipboard/caret requirements, coverage baselines, GitHub-only validation, independent reviews and full visual gate. Retain RPi policy/restart work and monitoring of every task-related PR through successful dev merge and required validation. This choice supplies no plan, code, visual, merge or protected exact-head approval.","questions":["1. Which correction should the renewed plan specify for the four unmounted-reset failures at head a30ce3df206677c416b34e06b99e97e80764d1f1?\nActive app context (Recommended): Run the existing parameterized test through asyncio.run and SqlExplorerApp(FakeSession()).run_test(); keep both new editors detached, explicitly assert they remain unmounted, preserve every construction/reset/history assertion, and leave production behavior unchanged."]},{"choice":"native_caret_correction: Native styling (Recommended)\nReason: The authenticated whitespace correction requires preserving every in-document character, expanded-tab cell, color and width while using thin underlines, with bars reserved for padding. Neutralizing native cursor styling after CSS resolution, preserving original theme state and retaining strict real-renderer assertions directly supports that requirement; inspected published-head PNGs still show block styling. Behavior-preserving formatting and reconciliation with pinned dev also support fixing encountered issues: current controller/documentation diffs remove newer provenance and notification safeguards, which must be preserved. Retain the complete multicursor, clipboard, history and narrow UI checkpoint, coverage/debt baselines, GitHub-only execution, fresh independent plan and implementation reviews, exact-head CI and all 46 geometry/full-PNG verdicts. Historical captures do not validate saved edits. Preserve companion policy/restart work and monitoring of every task-related PR through successful dev merge and required validation. Any remaining protected-path change requires the real owner's applicable exact-head approval; this choice supplies none.","questions":["1. Should the renewed plan correct native primary-caret styling before the existing underline overlay, retain strict real-renderer color assertions, fix the reported formatting, and reconcile stale controller/test/documentation changes with pinned dev while preserving the complete feature?\nNative styling (Recommended): Neutralize native cursor colors through a render-only theme after CSS resolution, preserve original theme state and cell colors, strengthen mounted regressions, and require fresh independent review plus GitHub CI and all 46 visual scenes."]}],"images":[],"plans":[{"approval_index":0,"id":"cf25c1a4d6a8bb36186ff70e6f5ad9dd930414b0e4e2a7426f5a5236986ba29a","text":"# SQL Explorer selection, multicursor clipboard, and thin carets\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd continuous selection with Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down, reproduce VS Code’s multicursor paste distribution, and render every editor caret as a thin vertical bar. Keep your explicit override: empty selections copy empty fragments.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Bind Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down to extend each existing selection by one logical line without adding cursors. Preserve its anchor and preferred column, clamp on short lines, and restore that column on longer lines. Reversing direction shrinks the selection and can cross its anchor. Keep Shift+Up/Down as the existing add-cursor shortcuts.\n- Store multicursor clipboard metadata alongside the plain clipboard text: one fragment per selection in document order, including empty fragments and embedded newlines. Export joined plain text through the existing system clipboard and OSC 52 transports.\n- Follow [VS Code’s paste distribution](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/main/src/vs/editor/common/cursor/cursorTypeEditOperations.ts): distribute stored fragments when their count matches the destination cursor count; otherwise distribute clipboard lines when their count matches, ignoring one trailing line ending. If neither matches, insert the whole clipboard at every cursor. A single destination receives the joined text.\n- Apply fragments by destination document order, rather than attaching them permanently to cursor identities. Invalidate stored metadata on another Explorer copy or when received clipboard text differs.\n- Route Ctrl+C/Ctrl+V, `cp`/`pst`, cut, and terminal paste through shared clipboard handling. Leave query execution’s selected-text collection separate. Copying with all selections empty clears the clipboard; pasting an empty clipboard does nothing.\n- Extend the existing batch-edit mechanism to accept distinct insertions while preserving cursor positions and one-step undo/redo.\n- Replace block caret rendering with a non-bold vertical bar for active and secondary cursors, including unfocused, empty-line, and end-of-line carets. The bar temporarily covers its terminal cell without changing document text.\n- Update Explorer’s editing documentation and add the required changelog fragment. No public package API changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Test repeated vertical selection, direction reversal, short/empty lines, document boundaries, existing multicursors, and unchanged add-cursor shortcuts.\n- Test distinct and multiline fragments, mixed/all-empty selections, changed cursor counts, recreated cursors, external line spreading, full-text fallback, clipboard replacement, and single-cursor paste.\n- Verify keyboard, command, cut, terminal-paste, clipboard-fallback, and undo/redo paths.\n- Verify bar carets with syntax highlighting, selections, scrolling, and focus changes.\n- Run focused and mandatory precommit checks. Complete the full SQL Explorer headless visual review, inspecting every scene before commit.\n\n## Delivery and defaults\n\nAfter leaving Plan mode, create the session-owned feature branch through the managed workflow and revalidate against incoming changes. Implement, validate, and publish a PR to `dev`.\n\nVS Code parity applies to the requested selection and clipboard behavior; retain existing Explorer shortcuts. Your empty-selection rule takes precedence over VS Code’s default line-copy behavior.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"48a661e2fd3a2309b243f9ec0fb10cf92f3d305e7ad8d345b1de83600ff2c620","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and complete picker diagnosis on current dev\n\n## Summary\n\nRevalidate the complete saved correction against pinned dev `0b26a608bba00ff1bf29bde578b436aa817eab14`. Preserve the multicursor feature and useful checkpoint changes, resolve both merge conflicts through the approved coder, and validate the already-selected four-way picker comparison.\n\nNo additional owner choices are needed for this step. The verified PNG shows an obscured `c`; the supplied SVGs retain the complete heading. The rendering cause remains unproven, so this plan authorizes diagnosis, not a speculative presentation repair.\n\n## Merge recovery and compatibility\n\n- In `.github/agent/task_context.py`, resolve both conflicts to the pinned base’s behavior: retain `Path`, `ARCHIVE_MARKER`, and oversized inline evidence returning `None` so publication can use the archive transport. The resolved file should match pinned dev exactly; preserve complete history and existing provenance checks.\n- In `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, combine both sides of both conflicts, retaining distinct feature and current-dev entries and all historical release sections. Remove only conflict markers and exact duplicate entries.\n- Retain the existing task fragment as one concise `- ` bullet; it already satisfies the reported format requirement. Do not change package or README versions.\n- Preserve recovered diagnostic tests and README content. Fully read files before editing; compare against the immutable pre24 originals and retain every original test method, the recovered suffix, and useful diagnostic additions.\n- Preserve public package APIs, existing creation shortcuts, clipboard transports, and supported Python/Textual compatibility. The picker comparison is an additive diagnostic JSON interface.\n\n## Feature requirements to retain\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without adding cursors, preserving independent preferred columns through short lines, reversal, and boundaries.\n- Support independent cursor positions, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, editing, and one-step undo/redo. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard; cut deletes nothing. One unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Paste uses matching recorded fragments first, matching clipboard lines second, and whole-text repetition otherwise. Ignore one trailing line ending for line spreading. Keyboard, command, and terminal paste share these rules; changed clipboard text invalidates fragment metadata.\n- Keep SQL readable: supported vertical bars where possible, thin underlines in occupied cells, and visible primary and secondary carets.\n- Retain only the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs: scene consistency and Cancel focus, create-table controls and menu placement, help wrapping, find-highlight visibility, and evidence-led picker diagnosis.\n\n## Diagnostic implementation and focused coverage\n\nPreserve and finish the existing integration between `agent_tools/sql_explorer_svg_evidence.py` and `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_capture.py`, with regressions in `tests/agent_tools/svg_evidence.py`.\n\n- For database-picker only, retain `raw_original`, `framed_original`, `raw_dejavu`, and `framed_dejavu` in geometry JSON from one final export. Reuse the ordinary PNG for `framed_original`.\n- Change only the terminal matrix font-family declaration in diagnostic font variants to verified-available DejaVu Sans Mono. Preserve production rendering, text, positions, clips, title fonts, and framing.\n- Retain exact UTF-8 SVG strings, lossless base64 PNGs, lengths, SHA256 hashes, observed dimensions, renderer arguments, versions, and font observations.\n- Keep separate 4 MiB combined comparison SVG and decoded PNG limits. Missing fonts, ambiguous declarations, renderer failures, or omitted content must mark comparisons incomplete. System font matches must never be described as renderer-selected fonts.\n- Keep atomic geometry publication and the existing artifact route; do not modify the protected capture workflow.\n- Run fast, service-free regressions covering lossless encoding, exact boundaries, unavailable/fallback fonts, declaration-only changes, partial failures, ordinary-PNG reuse, picker-only integration, and preserved geometry/readiness gates.\n- Recheck multicursor, selection/clipboard, caret, button-style, selector, completion, and capture-lifecycle suites. Historical CI identified disabled-button color failures and lint findings; verify their current corrections on the new candidate without weakening assertions or debt baselines.\n\n## GitHub validation and completion\n\n- Private planning/coding workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering. GitHub performs focused checks, mandatory static/coverage/artifact/matrix validation, and captures.\n- Obtain independent plan review covering the new base, both conflict resolutions, and the complete preserved task before coding.\n- Use the trusted isolated candidate route to capture all 46 scenes and the four picker comparisons. Bind artifacts to the exact candidate, checkpoint, task, and plan; coordinator extraction must verify decoded bytes and hashes.\n- Independently inspect all four comparison images before selecting a repair. Incomplete or inconclusive comparisons require further diagnosis and renewed planning. A successful capture is not visual approval.\n- Once evidence establishes the cause, obtain a concrete reviewed repair plan, add a focused regression, and repeat full-scene capture. Every geometry assertion and individual full-PNG verdict must pass before correction publication.\n- Require fresh implementation review and required checks for the final published head and current dev base. Preserve credentials, owner vetoes, provenance, and any applicable exact-head protected approval.\n- The coordinator retains responsibility for recommendation-policy companion review, safe activation, and recovery of waiting agents while preserving genuine-input/security holds.\n- Monitor SQL Explorer PR #9, the recommendation-policy/restart companion work, and all task-related repair PRs through successful dev merges and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that root objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"7ff002c5964b2e8a254e39d777cc20399ff3b70586fc5e3cc917aedf80f0f827","text":"# Correct PR #9 CI while preserving SQL Explorer requirements\n\n## Summary\n\nCorrect the failures bound to head `0a943f8c16643228436a2bcbc23b02fbe2f28cff` in GitHub run `38889674199`, against pinned dev `0b26a608bba00ff1bf29bde578b436aa817eab14`.\n\nThe immutable logs establish two causes: invalid plain-color parsing in the disabled-button regression and new Ruff findings in the SVG diagnostic helper/tests. The resolver selected the CSS-reference approach; that selection supplies no implementation, visual, or protected-policy approval.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `tests/sql/explorer/button_styles.py`, remove the `Color.parse(palette[\"text-disabled\"])` override from `DisabledColorReference`. Let its existing `color: $text-disabled` CSS resolve through Textual after mounting beside the tested button.\n- Retain strict comparisons of resolved foreground/background, automatic-color state, and rendered Rich foreground/background. Preserve the deliberate incorrect-color negative control, cleanup, hover/focus checks, removal-control legibility, and both advanced-panel states.\n- In `agent_tools/sql_explorer_svg_evidence.py`, correct the reported FURB167, PERF401, two PLR2004 findings, and unused RUF100 suppression using equivalent expressions, named limits, and removal of only the unused suppression. Preserve iteration order and exact diagnostic contents.\n- In `tests/agent_tools/svg_evidence.py`, fix all four E501 findings and Ruff formatting through layout changes and adjacent string literals that preserve fixture bytes. Retain every test and assertion.\n- Keep public APIs, dependency declarations, Python 3.8–3.14 support, supported Textual versions, diagnostic schema/version, hashes, encodings, and separate 4 MiB SVG/decoded-PNG limits unchanged. Preserve the existing changelog history and record the correction through the managed fragment mechanism without a package-version bump.\n- Fully read each edited file through `has_more=false`; preserve recovered diagnostic tests, documentation, and the complete checkpoint. Do not reset the feature or modify lint/type debt baselines.\n\n## Requirements retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without spawning cursors, preserving independent preferred columns through short lines, reversal, and boundaries.\n- Retain independent cursor positions, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, batch editing, and one-step undo/redo. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard; cut deletes nothing. One unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command, and terminal paste distribute matching fragments first, matching lines second—ignoring one trailing line ending—and otherwise repeat the whole text. Changed clipboard text invalidates metadata; empty paste does nothing.\n- Preserve readable SQL and visible primary/secondary thin carets: supported vertical bars where possible, thin underlines in occupied cells.\n- Retain the selected narrow fixture/UI repairs and evidence-led picker diagnosis. Preserve four-way raw/framed, original/DejaVu comparison evidence, ordinary-PNG reuse, atomic geometry publication, and explicit incomplete results. This CI correction does not select a picker presentation or rasterization repair.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub; private workers only inspect or edit source.\n\n- First run the button-style module on minimum and current Textual environments. Require both advanced-panel states to pass for every button, with strict rendered-color comparisons and negative controls still detecting incorrect colors.\n- Run SVG-evidence tests with fake font probes/renderers: verify exact bytes/hashes, font-declaration-only changes, exact limit boundaries, unavailable/fallback fonts, partial failures, PNG dimensions, ordinary-PNG reuse, picker-only integration, and readiness/geometry rejection.\n- Run focused multicursor, selection/clipboard, movement, caret, selector/completion, and capture-lifecycle regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head static/lint/format/type checks, coverage ratchets, artifact smoke tests, Python compatibility/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK conformance, and the aggregate fast-check gate. Preserve all assertions and baselines.\n- Use the trusted isolated candidate route for full-scene capture. Bind artifacts to candidate, checkpoint, task, plan, and reviewed content; independently inspect all 46 full PNGs and require every geometry assertion and individual verdict to pass before correction publication.\n- Preserve the picker comparison review prerequisite wherever unresolved. Successful capture or green CI alone does not establish its cause or visual approval; a demonstrated repair requires a concrete renewed plan, focused regression, and full visual review.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before coding, then independent implementation review for the resulting head and current dev base. Revalidate if dev changes.\n- Preserve complete authenticated task history and provenance through trusted publication transport. Coordinator tooling gaps remain coordinator-owned; do not truncate history.\n- Keep protected workflows unchanged for this correction. Any later protected-path change requires the real owner’s applicable exact-head approval; recommendation selection cannot substitute.\n- The coordinator must complete the RPi recommendation-policy companion work and safely restart agents waiting solely on routine implementation choices, preserving genuine-input, credential, provenance, and owner-veto holds.\n- Continue monitoring PR #9, the RPi policy/restart companion PRs, and every task-related correction/repair PR until all merge successfully into dev and required post-merge validation completes. This bounded CI correction does not complete that root objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"b3631dec6cfa7592c57086a4b15a7092ff53c6453c44ec3db30371479476aa73","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and complete the evidence-first correction\n\n## Summary\n\nRevalidate the complete saved patch against pinned dev `43edcf11550c28f42645c15a92e41b8f4340d0c1`. Only the approved coder may resolve conflicts or edit source.\n\nPreserve the selected evidence-first sequence: reconcile the changelog, finish behavior-preserving lint corrections and bounded diagnostics, then obtain exact-candidate GitHub evidence before specifying a production checkbox or picker repair. No additional owner decision is needed for this step.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- Resolve every conflict in `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, including the new top conflict and nested older markers. Use pinned dev’s release history as the skeleton; retain all distinct feature and dev entries, removing conflict markers and exact duplicate entries only. Preserve historical release sections and package/README versions.\n- Preserve the complete feature checkpoint, recovered test/documentation content, authenticated chronological history, and existing task fragment. Fully read each file through its final page before editing.\n- In `agent_tools/sql_explorer_svg_evidence.py`, verify the saved correction addresses the reported BLE001/RUF100 findings while retaining renderer-failure containment and explicit incomplete evidence. Apply canonical formatting to its tests without changing fixture bytes, diagnostic contents, limits, hashes, or assertions.\n- Retain the existing checkbox diagnostics and regressions, particularly `tests/agent_tools/checkbox_diagnostics.py`. On strict form assertion failure, report the original snapshot without recollecting: checkbox value/label, direct render, widget/compositor rows, styles, ancestor geometry/clips, advanced-panel state, and runtime versions. Keep output bounded and explicitly identify missing or truncated observations.\n- Preserve public package interfaces, Python 3.8–3.14 and supported Textual compatibility. Diagnostic JSON remains additive. Do not change dependencies, protected workflows, coverage targets, debt baselines, production checkbox presentation, or picker rendering in this diagnostic step.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without creating cursors; preserve independent preferred columns, reversal, short lines, and boundaries.\n- Retain multiple cursors per row, selection merging, movement, batch editing, atomic undo/redo, and Shift+Up/Down toggling at the exact projected position.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp`, and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments, including empty fragments. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Paste distributes matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, and otherwise repeats the whole text. Keyboard, command, and terminal paste share the rules; changed clipboard text invalidates metadata.\n- Preserve readable SQL and visible thin primary/secondary carets: vertical bars where supported,